# Introduction
Traffic Lights is a domain with a lot of variability across the different jurisdictions around the world. 
In this wiki, we are gradually building a variability model of this domain using a modeling language 

[ ![Clafer logo](http://t3-necsis.cs.uwaterloo.ca:8091/img/logo.png) ](http://clafer.org)

We explain the modeling language and the supporting tools along the way.

This material is based on Wikipedia [Traffic Light](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light) and [Traffic Light Variations](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_variations_in_traffic_light_signalling_and_operation) articles. 
The content is prepared by Michał Antkiewicz [email](mailto:mantkiew@gsd.uwaterloo.ca), [home](http://gsd.uwaterloo.ca/mantkiew).

You can always return to this front page by clicking on the traffic lights logo in the top-left corner.

